@AdrianoCP Great! Glad you're liking!

#1 - By default the max width of the bar is your current health. So lets say you max health is 100, and the absorb on you is 50, it will fill the bar exactly half way. About using the shield's full health - that is unfortunately not possible - the in-game API does not expose this information at all, the only thing the ap returns is the total absorb shield value on a unit (not even from what sources, which could be used to narrow this down). In any case, I've added an issue to investigate and see what's possible here: https://github.com/tusharsaxena/AbsorbTracker/issues/15

#2 - I can add that for sure, let me look into this. I think for some classes it would be useful (e.g. mage) but some classes keep on continuously getting and depleting shields (Blood DK for example) so it would be super spammy. Can add this as an opt-in feature though. I'll look into to the TTS bit, I think it should be doable. Good suggestion, thank you!. Tracking this here: https://github.com/tusharsaxena/AbsorbTracker/issues/16

8225824.text:
@AdrianoCP I looked into it this a bit more, and unfortunately addons can't do this in Midnight. In TWW it was easy: read the absorb value, check for zero, play a sound. 12.0 wraps that value up as a "secret value" - we can't read it or compare it. Blizz did add ways to respond to secrets, but all of them are visual (bar fills and color changes). There's no audio version.

The two workarounds that used to work pre-Midnight are gone as well: combat log access was pulled from addons entirely in 12.0, and aura data goes secret the moment a raid encounter, M+ key or PvP match starts. Which is when you'd actually want the alert.

I could build a version that works out in the world and stays silent in raids and dungeons, but that seems pretty pointless to be honest. Blizzard's own Combat Audio Alerts and the Cooldown Manager sound alerts in the base UI are the closest thing for now. If they ever give us a sound trigger that works with secrets, or an event for SHIELD_DEPLETED or something like that, I'd be happy revisit this.
